{'symbol': 'FICO', 'date': '2022-12-15 04:00:00', 'title': "SURVEY: UK CONSUMERS ACCEPT MORE IDENTITY CHECKS AFTER LOSSES OF £15.3M ACROSS CHRISTMAS '21", 'text': 'LONDON--( BUSINESS WIRE )--THERE WAS A REPORTED £15.3 MILLION LOST TO FRAUD IN THE UK BETWEEN NOVEMBER 2021 AND JANUARY 2022, AND WITH JUST A FEW DAYS UNTIL CHRISTMAS DAY, PANIC MODE COULD BE SETTING IN THIS YEAR. THE GOOD NEWS IS THAT IT APPEARS UK SHOPPERS RECOGNIZE THE IMPORTANCE OF INCREASED FRAUD CHECKS BY LENDERS AND BANKS. GLOBAL ANALYTICS SOFTWARE COMPANY FICO HAS REVEALED THE FINDINGS FROM ITS LATEST SURVEYI WITH CONSUMERS SHOWING AN INCREASED UNDERSTANDING OF HOW AND WHY FRAUD CHECKS NEED TO HAPPEN. SHOPPERS ARE ALSO EMBRACING BIOMETRICS TO ADD LAYERS OF PROTECTION TO THEIR ACCOUNTS.'}